[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   Step 138: One-way downlink channel audit (step_b102).
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   Registers the one-way-transport channel the two-way cancellation
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   theorem requires.  In a two-way radio link traversing a
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   proper-time (lapse) gradient, the round trip traverses the same
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   gradient twice with opposite sign in the observable transport and
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   the lapse term cancels; a one-way downlink referenced to an
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   onboard oscillator does not cancel.  This step audits which
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   one-way deep-space datasets exist, what distances they cover, and
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   whether a TEP-sensitive residual product can be built from them.
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   T1  Transport-class mapping: the onboard-oscillator-referenced
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   one-way carrier is the required observable class.  The GNSS
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   satellite-to-receiver downlink is the same class -- atomic-
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   clock referenced, uplink-free -- so the corpus already
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   realizes the one-way test through the GNSS-II clock
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   correlation channel (step 135 / b99: free axis 0.6 deg from
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   the comet meridian plane).
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   T2  Deep-space archive inventory:
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   - Voyager delta-VLBI demonstration, 1979 Jupiter approach
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   (22 of 25 scheduled passes usable; goal 50 nrad, achieved
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   ~0.5 urad scatter; AIAA 82-1471; IPN PR 42-60) and the
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   Saturn-era delta-DOR measurements via the 360 kHz telemetry
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   subcarrier.  Downlink-only mode, 5-10 AU.  Observables not
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   in a public machine-readable archive.
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   - Cassini VLBA astrometry (published position solutions;
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   raw delay observables not publicly archived).
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   - PRIDE Venus Express / Mars Express open-loop one-way
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   tracking (EVN, AuScope, NICT; X-band USO-referenced;
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   mHz-level Doppler products; raw correlator-level data at
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   the EVN archive; processed products in the published
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   record).  Inner-system paths (<<2 AU).
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   T3  Boundary-distance coverage: the candidate lapse boundary sits
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   at heliospheric distances and beyond (>=100 AU).  None of the
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   public one-way archives reaches beyond ~10 AU; at 150+ AU the
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   Voyager carrier is receivable only by 70-m-class apertures and
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   no public VLBI record exists there.  Registered: no public
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   one-way dataset covers the boundary-distance regime.
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   T4  Sensitivity ordering: the 1979 delta-VLBI pass scatter
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   (~0.5 urad, ~few ns differential delay) against the
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   GNSS-class one-way clock sensitivity already exploited in the
[2026-09-20 12:25:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 138]   corpus -- ordering the channels by realized reach.
